---
/**
 * Supporting Editorial Content for JPG to HEIC Converter
 *
 * Provides educational context on the HEIC container format, compression advantages,
 * realistic limitations, and 100% client-side privacy assurances.
 */
---

<div class="space-y-14 mb-14">
  <!-- 1. What is HEIC? -->
  <section aria-labelledby="what-is-heic-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          i
        </div>
        <h2 id="what-is-heic-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
          What is HEIC?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-surface-600 leading-relaxed max-w-none">
        <p>
          HEIC (High Efficiency Image Container) is an image container format based on the High Efficiency Image File Format (HEIF) specification developed by the Moving Picture Experts Group (MPEG). It leverages advanced High Efficiency Video Coding (HEVC / H.265) intra-frame compression techniques to store high-resolution image data at substantially lower file sizes compared to legacy JPEG images.
        </p>
        <p>
          Widely adopted as the primary photo capture format on modern Apple iPhone and iPad devices, HEIC supports rich features such as 16-bit color depth, auxiliary depth maps, HDR image data, and multiple image bursts within a single compact file container.
        </p>
        <p>
          Converting your JPG images to HEIC allows you to store and organize personal photo libraries using modern high-efficiency standards. Need the opposite conversion? You can always use our companion tool to <a href="/image/heic-to-jpg" class="text-brand-600 font-medium underline decoration-brand-300 underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-700 transition-colors">convert HEIC to JPG</a> at any time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Why convert JPG to HEIC? -->
  <section aria-labelledby="why-convert-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-3">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          ⇄
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 id="why-convert-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
            Why convert JPG to HEIC?
          </h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 mt-0.5">Key advantages and practical scenarios for converting images to HEIC</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-6">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span>
            Storage Optimization
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            HEIC utilizes sophisticated spatial prediction and advanced quantization to store image data more efficiently than standard JPEG, helping reduce long-term archive sizes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span>
            Apple Ecosystem Harmony
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            If you maintain a photo library on macOS, iOS, or iCloud, keeping your images in native HEIC format ensures seamless synchronization with Apple Photos workflows.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span>
            Photo Sharing & Bandwidth
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Smaller file sizes consume less mobile data and upload faster when transferring photo collections over messaging platforms that support native HEIF previewing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span>
            Developer & QA Testing
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Generate authentic ISO BMFF HEIF image containers directly from standard JPEG test assets without needing specialized native command-line toolchains or macOS hardware.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. How to convert JPG to HEIC -->
  <section aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          ✓
        </div>
        <h2 id="how-it-works-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
          How to convert JPG to HEIC
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mt-4">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <span class="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-brand-100 text-brand-700 text-xs font-bold mb-2">Step 1</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1">Select or Drop JPGs</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Pick one or more .jpg or .jpeg images from your computer or mobile device. Files stay entirely in your local browser memory.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <span class="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-brand-100 text-brand-700 text-xs font-bold mb-2">Step 2</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1">Select Quality Level</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Fine-tune the output quality slider between 50% and 100%. Our recommended 85% default balances high visual fidelity with optimal compression.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <span class="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-brand-100 text-brand-700 text-xs font-bold mb-2">Step 3</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1">Download HEIC Files</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Download your genuine .heic files individually or grab the entire converted batch bundled into a single ZIP file.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Browser and file limitations -->
  <section aria-labelledby="limitations-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          !
        </div>
        <h2 id="limitations-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
          Browser and file limitations
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-surface-600 leading-relaxed max-w-none">
        <p>
          <strong>No quality restoration:</strong> Converting a JPG to HEIC cannot recover visual detail, dynamic range, or clarity that was already lost during the original JPEG compression. HEIC stores the available pixel data with modern efficiency, but cannot undo historical artifacts.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Heavy CPU & memory requirements:</strong> HEIC encoding uses complex HEVC intra-frame prediction algorithms that require significant processing power and device RAM. To prevent browser memory exhaustion, images are encoded sequentially.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Variable size reduction:</strong> While HEIC is inherently more efficient than standard JPEG, already heavily compressed or low-resolution JPGs may see minimal file size reduction when re-encoded.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>EXIF metadata stripping:</strong> In-browser pixel decoding through standard HTML5 canvas APIs normalizes image orientation and strips embedded EXIF camera settings, timestamps, and GPS coordinates for enhanced online privacy.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Legacy compatibility:</strong> Although HEIC is natively supported on modern Apple and Android devices, older desktop operating systems (e.g. Windows 7/8 or unconfigured Windows 10/11 installations) may require third-party codec extensions to view .heic files.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. Client-Side Privacy Guarantee -->
  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-emerald-50/60 border border-emerald-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-3">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          🔒
        </div>
        <h2 id="privacy-heading" class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-emerald-950">
          Client-Side Privacy Guarantee
        </h2>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-emerald-900/90 leading-relaxed">
        Unlike traditional online converters that upload your personal photographs to remote cloud servers for conversion, our tool executes 100% inside your browser using WebAssembly. Your photos never leave your device, no telemetry is gathered, and no copies are saved anywhere on the internet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
